{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781563467445,"sessionID":"ses_1328b9ab2ffeOhczfsgewRmTkz","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_hXcb9Uk7l3aORf0B3KxIEq9E","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n+## Policy Selection Checkpoint\n+\n+- Controlling policy source: `current_policy.md`\n+- Current policy date: 2026-04-20\n+- Trip dates being audited: 2026-05-08 to 2026-05-10\n+- Why this policy controls: the current policy is effective for trips starting on or after 2026-05-01, this trip started on 2026-05-08, and the current policy explicitly supersedes older policy excerpts for covered trips.\n+- Why the stale excerpt does not control: `stale_policy_excerpt.md` is dated 2026-03-01 and says it may be stale if a newer policy applies.\n+\n+## Rules Applied Checkpoint\n+\n+- Receipt threshold: receipts are required for every expense of $75.00 or more.\n+- Seat-upgrade rule: seat upgrades, extra-legroom fees, priority boarding, and similar optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is included in the receipt evidence.\n+- Lodging cap calculation basis: lodging is capped at $220.00 per covered night, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees. Covered nights are 2, so the lodging cap is `2 x $220.00 = $440.00`.\n+- Meal and alcohol rule: meals are reimbursable at actual cost up to $65.00 per day, and alcohol is not reimbursable and must be removed from meal receipts.\n+- Ride-share tip cap: ride-share tips are reimbursable up to 20% of the base fare; any amount above that is not reimbursable.\n+- Supplies receipt rule: work supplies can be reimbursed only when a required receipt is provided and the business purpose is clear.\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\n+## Item-Level Audit Checkpoint\n+\n+| Expense ID | Claimed Amount | Approved Amount | Non-Reimbursable Amount | Status | Policy / Receipt Reason |\n+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n+| T-001 | $480.00 | $480.00 | $0.00 | approved | Economy airfare with receipt is reimbursable. |\n+| T-002 | $45.00 | $0.00 | $45.00 | rejected | Seat upgrade is not reimbursable without written preapproval; receipt shows no written preapproval. |\n+| T-003 | $510.00 | $440.00 | $70.00 | partial | Lodging cap is $220.00 per night for 2 covered nights, so reimbursement is capped at $440.00. |\n+| T-004 | $76.00 | $58.00 | $18.00 | partial | Meal receipt includes $18.00 of alcohol, which is not reimbursable; remaining $58.00 food cost is within the $65.00 daily meal cap. |\n+| T-005 | $70.00 | $60.00 | $10.00 | partial | Ride-share base fare of $50.00 is reimbursable; tip is capped at 20% of base fare, so only $10.00 of the $20.00 tip is reimbursable. |\n+| T-006 | $82.00 | $0.00 | $82.00 | rejected | Supplies expense is $75.00 or more, so a receipt is required; no receipt was provided. |\n+| T-007 | $18.00 | $18.00 | $0.00 | approved | Meal receipt is present, no alcohol is noted, and $18.00 is within the $65.00 daily meal cap. |\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md\n+## Reimbursement Summary Checkpoint\n+\n+- Reimbursable total: $1,056.00\n+- Non-reimbursable total: $225.00\n+- Reimbursable total calculation: `$480.00 + $0.00 + $440.00 + $58.00 + $60.00 + $0.00 + $18.00 = $1,056.00`\n+- Fully approved expense IDs: `T-001`, `T-007`\n+- Partially reimbursed or capped expense IDs: `T-003`, `T-004`, `T-005`\n+- Rejected expense IDs: `T-002`, `T-006`\n+\n+## Finance Notes\n+\n+- The current 2026-04-20 policy applies because the trip started on 2026-05-08, after the 2026-05-01 effective date.\n+- The largest reductions came from the lodging cap, alcohol exclusion on the dinner receipt, the ride-share tip cap, the non-reimbursable seat upgrade, and the missing receipt for supplies.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\nA tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\nA tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n+++ /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@\n+## Policy Selection Checkpoint\n+\n+- Controlling policy source: `current_policy.md`\n+- Current policy date: 2026-04-20\n+- Trip dates being audited: 2026-05-08 to 2026-05-10\n+- Why this policy controls: the current policy is effective for trips starting on or after 2026-05-01, this trip started on 2026-05-08, and the current policy explicitly supersedes older policy excerpts for covered trips.\n+- Why the stale excerpt does not control: `stale_policy_excerpt.md` is dated 2026-03-01 and says it may be stale if a newer policy applies.\n+\n+## Rules Applied Checkpoint\n+\n+- Receipt threshold: receipts are required for every expense of $75.00 or more.\n+- Seat-upgrade rule: seat upgrades, extra-legroom fees, priority boarding, and similar optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is included in the receipt evidence.\n+- Lodging cap calculation basis: lodging is capped at $220.00 per covered night, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees. Covered nights are 2, so the lodging cap is `2 x $220.00 = $440.00`.\n+- Meal and alcohol rule: meals are reimbursable at actual cost up to $65.00 per day, and alcohol is not reimbursable and must be removed from meal receipts.\n+- Ride-share tip cap: ride-share tips are reimbursable up to 20% of the base fare; any amount abov